From bc41fdffa09dea3a58773d400253b208e124d0ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 05:44:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] doc,contrib: drop libevent from build instructions and
 packaging

libevent is no longer needed to build or run the node. Remove it from
the build instructions for macOS, Debian/Ubuntu, Fedora, Arch and the
Windows cross build, from the dependency table, the Chronik build
guide, the Debian build dependencies, the AUR package, the Chronik
plugins image and the bookworm dependency script.

The developer notes now describe the HTTP and Tor control threads as
Boost.Asio. The release notes say libevent is gone, that the libevent
log category is still accepted but does nothing, and list the two RPC
client changes (each address of a host name is tried; a zero
-rpcclienttimeout means no timeout).

electrum/ is left alone: it bundles its own Tor and never used the
node's libevent.

Tier: eCash
